    "result_text": "All tests pass (the suite has one test class, `AcceptanceTest`, plus base/helper classes) and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented soft-duplicate detection for `POST /api/owners`: when a new owner isn't a hard duplicate (unique identity key) but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* telephone, it's still created and flagged `possibleDuplicate: true` / `possibleDuplicateOf: <matching id>`; otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions, the logic lives in one small single-responsibility step rather than being bolted onto an existing class:\n\n1. **New function class** `AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate.java` \u2014 finds the earliest (lowest-id) existing owner with the same last name (case-insensitive), same postcode, and a different telephone, and sets the flags on the entity. Reuses `OwnerRepository.findByLastName` and mirrors the shape of the sibling `Assign*` steps. An owner with no postcode can't match.\n\n2. **Pipeline wiring** (`owners.POST.yml`) \u2014 inserted `assignPossibleDuplicate` right after `ensureUniqueIdentityKey` (so hard duplicates are already rejected) and before `save` (so the flags persist), under the same `transaction` governance.\n\n3. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added persisted `possibleDuplicate` (boolean, `NOT NULL`) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (`Integer`) columns with accessors, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns them after JPA reload.\n\n4. **Schema DDL** \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb \u2014 the test DB, plus h2, postgres, mysql).\n\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the two `readOnly` properties to the `Owner` response schema; MapStruct then carries them through `toOwnerDto` automatically (no mapper edits needed).",
